t involving EHA\",\"time_scope\":\"project timeline\",\"explanation\":\"none\",\"fields\":[\"funding_program\",\"start_date\",\"duration\"]},\"program_revision\":0,\"rule_binding\":null,\"supported_parents\":{},\"known_observations\":[],\"source_spans\":[[\"s45\",\"d1\",0,389,\"ASCERTAIN – IMPROVING ACCESS TO INNOVATIVE HEALTH TECHNOLOGIES\\nASCERTAIN – IMPROVING ACCESS TO INNOVATIVE HEALTH TECHNOLOGIES\\nASCERTAIN Project\\nAbout\\nImpact\\nWork Packages\\nConsortium\\nAdvisory Board\\nFinal Conference\\nNews & Events\\nFor Patients\\nResults\\nContact\\nEnglish\\nDeutsch (German)\\nNorsk bokmål (Norwegian Bokmål)\\nRomână (Romanian)\\nHrvatski (Croatian)\\nFrançais (French)\\nNederlands (Dutch)\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s46\",\"d1\",389,458,\"Español (Spanish)\\nIMPROVING ACCESS TO\\nINNOVATIVE HEALTH TECHNOLOGIES\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s47\",\"d1\",458,857,\"ASCERTAIN (Affordability and Sustainability improvements through new pricing, Cost- Effectiveness and ReimbursemenT models to Appraise INnovative health technologies) addresses the need of patients, physicians, payers, regulators, and manufacturers to improve the affordability and accessibility to innovative health technologies (including pharmaceuticals) in Europe.\\nFind out how you can benefit!\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s48\",\"d1\",857,1089,\"JOIN US FOR OUR FINAL CONFERENCE\\n21. October 2026 in Brussels\\nFrom Evidence to Access: Rethinking Healthcare Decision-Making in Europe\\nAs the ASCERTAIN project comes to a close, we are pleased to invite you to our Final Conference. \",\"document\",[]],[\"s49\",\"d1\",1089,1321,\"The event will bring together policymakers, HTA bodies, payers, patient representatives, industry, researchers, and healthcare professionals to explore new approaches to improving access to innovative health technologies in Europe.\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s50\",\"d1\",1321,1540,\"Throughout the day, participants will discover ASCERTAIN’s novel pricing, cost-effectiveness, and reimbursement models, developed to support more transparent, evidence-based, and sustainable healthcare decision-making. \",\"document\",[]],[\"s51\",\"d1\",1540,1870,\"These approaches will be showcased through the project’s three healthcare use cases – personalised cancer medicines, CAR T-cell therapies, and Next Generation Sequencing (NGS) tests for precision oncology – as well as the open-access Policy Support Tool that integrates these models into a practical decision-support environment.\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s52\",\"d1\",1870,2161,\"Held at The Dominican in Brussels, the conference will provide a forum for dialogue, collaboration, and reflection on the future of equitable access, affordability, and healthcare innovation in Europe.\\nAttendance at the conference is free of charge.\\nMore Info\\nBooking\\nFAQ\\nWhat is ASCERTAIN?\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s53\",\"d1\",2161,2477,\"ASCERTAIN is a project aimed at helping people get better access to new health technologies such as medicines, medical devices, and tests. The project is creating a tool that can be used by decision-makers to understand the cost and value of these new health technologies.\\nWhat is the ASCERTAIN policy support tool?\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s54\",\"d1\",2477,2866,\"The tool will be accessible to everyone on the internet and will have information about the cost and value of these new health technologies. It will also consider the impact on the environment. The project will work with patients, industry, policy makers, and payers to make sure the tool is good quality and useful.\\nWhy is the affordability of innovative health technologies a challenge?\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s55\",\"d1\",2866,3243,\"It’s a challenge for many countries in the European Union to afford new health technologies because they are often expensive and not everyone has equal access to them. This tool will help decision-makers understand how much a technology should cost, the added value it provides for patients, and its potential impact on the health care budget.\\nWhat are the goals of ASCERTAIN?\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s56\",\"d1\",3243,3642,\"The goal of ASCERTAIN is to make it easier for people to understand the cost and value of new health technologies. The tool will be open to everyone and will be able to be adapted to different countries’ needs. It will have information about the cost and value of these technologies and will encourage “greener” production.\\nWOULD YOU PREFER TO READ THIS PAGE IN A DIFFERENT LANGUAGE?\\nEvents\\n21\\n-\\n21\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s57\",\"d1\",3642,4011,\"Oct\\nASCERTAIN Final Conference\\nFrom Evidence to Access: Rethinking Healthcare Decision-Making in Europe is the motto of our finale ASCERTAIN conference. Join us in Brussels this October.\\nVIDEO\\nNews\\nASCERTAIN NEWSLETTER 6\\nWelcome to the sixth edition of the ASCERTAIN newsletter!\\nRead more\\nASCERTAIN Position Papers on Pricing, Modelling and Reimbursement Now Available\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s58\",\"d1\",4011,4277,\"We are pleased to announce the publication of three ASCERTAIN position papers addressing key challenges in the pricing, assessment, and reimbursement of innovative health technologies.\\nRead more\\nNew ASCERTAIN Position Paper on Pricing Innovative Health Technologies\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s59\",\"d1\",4277,4541,\"ASCERTAIN has published a new position paper summarising key findings and recommendations from Work Package 4 on pricing innovative health technologies.\\nRead more\\nNew ASCERTAIN video series explains how medicines are priced, evaluated and made available in Europe\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s60\",\"d1\",4541,4840,\"ASCERTAIN has launched a new animated video series designed to make complex topics around medicine pricing, cost-effectiveness, reimbursement, and decision-making in the European Union easier to understand.\\nRead more\\nNew ASCERTAIN Video Series: How Are Medicines Priced and What Makes a Price Fair?\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s61\",\"d1\",4840,5164,\"We have launched a new series of short educational videos exploring how medicines are priced, how prices are regulated, and how patient perspectives shape decisions on access.\\nRead more\\nASCERTAIN NEWSLETTER 5\\nWelcome to the fifth edition of the ASCERTAIN newsletter! This edition highlights how that vision is taking shape. \",\"document\",[]],[\"s62\",\"d1\",5164,5544,\"In our interview, Professor Tomas Tesar and Dr Mirjana Huic discuss cost-effectiveness thresholds and the challenge of balancing innovation with equity. Their insights echo ASCERTAIN’s wider mission — ensuring that value assessments reflect both scientific and societal priorities.\\nRead more\\nPresentation of New HTA Methodological Guideline for Slovakia at the Ministry of Health\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s63\",\"d1\",5544,5872,\"On September 30th, the Slovak Ministry of Health hosted a seminar presenting the new national HTA methodological guideline, organized by Professor Tomáš Tesař, with contributions from ASCERTAIN and international experts highlighting the relevance of cost-effectiveness thresholds.\\nRead more\\nASCERTAIN Consortium Meeting in Oslo\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s64\",\"d1\",5872,6259,\"On 30 June 2025, the ASCERTAIN Consortium held its Stakeholder Day in Oslo, bringing together experts from academia, healthcare, industry, and policy to discuss sustainable access to innovative health technologies (IHTs). The event focused on refining access-based pricing, cost-effectiveness, and reimbursement models by aligning them with stakeholder needs and expectations.\\nRead more\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s65\",\"d1\",6259,6659,\"ASCERTAIN Website Now Available in 8 Languages\\nWe are happy to announce that the ASCERTAIN project website is now accessible in eight different languages:\\nEnglish, German, Dutch, Norwegian, Romanian, Croatian, Spanish, and French.\\nRead more\\nTake Part in Our Survey on Access-Based Pricing for Innovative Medicines\\nThis survey is part of the ASCERTAIN Project and will remain open until 18 July 2025.\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s66\",\"d1\",6659,7017,\"Read more\\nwatch our videos to learn more about the project\\nDiscover the making of the six-part series ‘3 Things About’. In six videos we aim to make complex issues more accessible, fostering a deeper understanding of the challenges and opportunities in topics around ASCERTAIN.\\n“3 Things About the Value of New Cancer Drugs” – The sixth video in our series! \",\"document\",[]],[\"s67\",\"d1\",7017,7345,\"This video explores how different stakeholders define the value of new cancer drugs.\\n“3 Things About Cost-Effectiveness” – The fifth video in our series! This video explores cost-effectiveness analysis—a key method for assessing if treatments provide good value.\\n3 Things About Reimbursement” is the fourth video in our series. \",\"document\",[]],[\"s68\",\"d1\",7345,7718,\"In this video, we explore the complexities of drug reimbursement—a key factor in ensuring patient access to new medicines.\\n“3 Things About Pricing Of New Drugs” – The third video in our series! In this video, we explore the factors that influence drug pricing — a crucial topic in healthcare affordability.\\n“3 Things About Tiered Pricing” – The second video in our series! \",\"document\",[]],[\"s69\",\"d1\",7718,8063,\"In this video, we break down the concept of tiered pricing—a strategy used to set different drug prices across countries and patient groups.\\n“3 Things About Market Access” – The first video in our series! In this video, we dive into the crucial concept of market access—a vital process for making new drugs and treatments available to patients.\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s70\",\"d1\",8063,8419,\"Discover how ASCERTAIN is tackling inequalities in access to healthcare technologies with our latest animated video! Learn about the project’s mission to improve affordability and sustainability while promoting innovation and considering environmental impacts.\\nWe are excited to share our video showcasing the launch of the ASCERTAIN project in Rotterdam! \",\"document\",[]]],\"required_scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"SUPPLY project involving EHA\",\"time_scope\":\"project timeline\"},\"rules_completion_required\":false,\"supported_task_outputs\":{},\"source_documents\":{\"d1\":{\"doc_id\":\"web-f9552075330dd435c5a02363\",\"time_metadata\":{}}},\"source_span_columns\":[\"id\",\"doc_id\",\"start\",\"end\",\"text\",\"source_role\",\"source_message_indices\"]}"}], "logical_call_index": 6, "response_format": "plain", "input_tokens_local": 6958, "output_token_reserve": 4096, "input_margin": 256, "max_model_len": 120000, "tokenization_request_sha256": "4c3d4f2a68b5f906fec4781a2e588cb74341c7b764b9d1fca70299bae62d9151", "tokenization_endpoint_sha256": "0ed12ee94b55bfdbc62fb247243af2d71aa1d7ea503f5f191605ae295c5ad94a", "token_count_is_estimate": false, "token_estimator_id": "deployment_vllm_chat_v1", "tokenizer_id": null, "add_generation_prompt": true, "tokenization_scope": "adapted_plain_text_chat_default_server_template", "token_accounting_note": "Deployment input count; model weights and tokenizer hash are not independently verified", "tokenization_wire_sha256": "bdd981781ec0d6fc0e4697525d79ff4e5ff4c0363bd7fc99365390be2f85558c", "raw_output": "{\n  \"slots\": [\n    {\n      \"variable\": \"funding_program\",\n      \"observations\": [],\n      \"unresolved\": [],\n      \"reading_status\": \"no_relevant_evidence\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"variable\": \"start_date\",\n      \"observations\": [],\n      \"unresolved\": [],\n      \"reading_status\": \"no_relevant_evidence\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"variable\": \"duration\",\n      \"observations\": [],\n      \"unresolved\": [],\n      \"reading_status\": \"no_relevant_evidence\"\n    }\n  ]\n}", "response_metadata": {"finish_reason": "stop", "refusal": null, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 6958, "total_tokens": 7081, "completion_tokens": 123, "prompt_tokens_details": null, "completion_tokens_details": {"re