s://ehaweb.org/clinical-practice\", \"text\": \"Clinical practice\", \"source_region\": \"navigation\", \"source_context\": {\"start\": 494, \"end\": 674, \"text\": \"EHA)\\nCongress\\nHemaSphere\\nAbout EHA\\nSearch\\nConnect & Network\\nClinical practice\\nEducation & Training\\nResearch & Innovation\\nJoin EHA\\nLogin\\nEHA2027 Congress\\nEHA2026 Congress\\nCongress a\"}}, {\"id\": \"l48\", \"source_doc_id\": \"web-66f1eb59d2a4a12d02055bd2\", \"url\": \"https://ehaweb.org/education-training\", \"text\": \"Education & Training\", \"source_region\": \"navigation\", \"source_context\": {\"start\": 512, \"end\": 692, \"text\": \"Sphere\\nAbout EHA\\nSearch\\nConnect & Network\\nClinical practice\\nEducation & Training\\nResearch & Innovation\\nJoin EHA\\nLogin\\nEHA2027 Congress\\nEHA2026 Congress\\nCongress archive\\nScientific \"}}, {\"id\": \"l49\", \"source_doc_id\": \"web-66f1eb59d2a4a12d02055bd2\", \"url\": \"https://ehaweb.org/research-innovation\", \"text\": \"Research & Innovation\", \"source_region\": \"navigation\", \"source_context\": {\"start\": 533, \"end\": 713, \"text\": \"ch\\nConnect & Network\\nClinical practice\\nEducation & Training\\nResearch & Innovation\\nJoin EHA\\nLogin\\nEHA2027 Congress\\nEHA2026 Congress\\nCongress archive\\nScientific meetings\\nMembership\\nE\"}}], \"supported_parent_doc_ids\": [], \"source_pages\": [{\"doc_id\": \"web-f9552075330dd435c5a02363\", \"title\": \"ASCERTAIN – IMPROVING ACCESS TO INNOVATIVE HEALTH TECHNOLOGIES\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 126, \"end\": 406, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 280}, {\"start\": 407, \"end\": 1727, \"excerpt_start\": 281, \"excerpt_end\": 1601}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"ASCERTAIN Project\\nAbout\\nImpact\\nWork Packages\\nConsortium\\nAdvisory Board\\nFinal Conference\\nNews & Events\\nFor Patients\\nResults\\nContact\\nEnglish\\nDeutsch (German)\\nNorsk bokmål (Norwegian Bokmål)\\nRomână (Romanian)\\nHrvatski (Croatian)\\nFrançais (French)\\nNederlands (Dutch)\\nEspañol (Spanish)\\nIMPROVING ACCESS TO\\nINNOVATIVE HEALTH TECHNOLOGIES\\nASCERTAIN (Affordability and Sustainability improvements through new pricing, Cost- Effectiveness and ReimbursemenT models to Appraise INnovative health technologies) addresses the need of patients, physicians, payers, regulators, and manufacturers to improve the affordability and accessibility to innovative health technologies (including pharmaceuticals) in Europe.\\nFind out how you can benefit!\\nJOIN US FOR OUR FINAL CONFERENCE\\n21. October 2026 in Brussels\\nFrom Evidence to Access: Rethinking Healthcare Decision-Making in Europe\\nAs the ASCERTAIN project comes to a close, we are pleased to invite you to our Final Conference. The event will bring together policymakers, HTA bodies, payers, patient representatives, industry, researchers, and healthcare professionals to explore new approaches to improving access to innovative health technologies in Europe.\\nThroughout the day, participants will discover ASCERTAIN’s novel pricing, cost-effectiveness, and reimbursement models, developed to support more transparent, evidence-based, and sustainable healthcare decision-making. These approaches will be showcased through the project’s three healthcare use cases – personalised cancer medicines, CAR T-cell therapies, and Next Generation Sequencing (NGS) tests for p\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-66f1eb59d2a4a12d02055bd2\", \"title\": \"ASCERTAIN project for better pricing and reimbursement models enters final phase - The European Hematology Association (EHA)ASCERTAIN project for better pricing and reimbursement models enters final phase - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4381, \"end\": 4440, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 59}, {\"start\": 4621, \"end\": 6162, \"excerpt_start\": 60, \"excerpt_end\": 1601}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Left Sidebar\\n3 min read · July 23, 2026\\nJuly 23, 2026\\nShare\\nASCERTAIN project for better pricing and reimbursement models enters final phase\\nThe ASCERTAIN project is entering its final phase, with the final conference taking place on October 21, 2026 in Brussels.\\nASCERTAIN – Affordability and Sustainability improvements through new pricing, Cost- Effectiveness and ReimbursemenT models to Appraise INnovative health technologies – is an EU funded project focused on improving the affordability and accessibility of innovative health technologies by developing a policy support tool. EHA is a consortium partner in the project, which aligns with our advocacy priority to promote affordable and equitable access to innovative therapies in hematology.\\nAccessibility and pricing of new health technologies in hematology\\nHigh prices of new health technologies impede access to treatments for many patients with blood disorders. Health systems face the challenge of facilitating patient access to new health technologies while ensuring the system’s financial sustainability and providing incentives for innovation. Together with Myeloma Patients Europe and patient organizations for PNH and Sickle Cell Disease, EHA is representing the hematology field in the development of the ASCERTAIN project.\\nThe ASCERTAIN policy support tool\\nThe ASCERTAIN policy support tool aims to contribute to better anticipating and calculating pricing, health technology assessment (HTA), and reimbursement conditions for innovative health technologies (IHTs). The tool is hosted on a web-based publicly accessible platform a\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-4cb5a6b1c84fb2fe0a4694b9\", \"title\": \"Empowering progress, knowledge, and partnership. - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Empowering progress, knowledge, and partnership. - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4142, \"end\": 5742, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 1600}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Empowering progress, knowledge, and partnership.\\nWelcome to Borderless Hematology.\\nEHA is the leading force in hematology, bringing the community together to share knowledge, collaborate, connect, and grow.\\nTogether we accelerate progress through education, science, and innovation. Together we improve patient outcomes and progress towards cures—across Europe and beyond.\\nTogether, the future of hematology is within our reach.\\nJoin us with membership that works for you or learn more about our story.\\nEHA2027 Congress\\nEuropean affairs\\nEHA Campus\\nGrants\\nSpecialized Working Groups\\nWhat’s new?\\nGo to overview\\nTuesday, September 29, 2026\\nEHA's Long-Term Advocacy for Hematology Achieves a Major Milestone\\nTuesday, September 22, 2026\\nInterview with EHA’s European Affairs Committee Member, Ariane Weinman\\nThursday, July 23, 2026\\nASCERTAIN project for better pricing and reimbursement models enters final phase\\nWednesday, July 22, 2026\\nInterview with EHA’s European Affairs Committee Member, Kate Morgan\\nMonday, July 6, 2026\\nPublication of EHA Annual General Meeting 2026 minutes\\nReady to join our community?\\nOur network is not just a professional association; it’s a community that nurtures growth, membership, and innovation in a manner that transcends geographical and intellectual borders. To us, this is Borderless Hematology.\\nJoin EHA today\\nEHA Mentorship Program\\nBecome a mentor today\\nMentoring is about more than sharing knowledge. It’s about building connections, gaining fresh perspectives, and helping shape the future of hematology.\\nIf you believe in the power of community and want to suppo\"}], \"local_exploration\": {\"visited_doc_ids\": [\"web-4cb5a6b1c84fb2fe0a4694b9\", \"web-66f1eb59d2a4a12d02055bd2\", \"web-f9552075330dd435c5a02363\"], \"visited_pages\": [{\"doc_id\": \"web-4cb5a6b1c84fb2fe0a4694b9\", \"url\": \"https://ehaweb.org/\", \"title\": \"Empowering progress, knowledge, and partnership. - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Empowering progress, knowledge, and partnership. - The Euro