 of ICSE\\n\"}}], \"supported_parent_doc_ids\": [], \"source_pages\": [{\"doc_id\": \"web-7b855fc9dc0c9e96e2068233\", \"title\": \"Organizing ICSE\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 32, \"end\": 1626, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 1594}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"ICSE\\nInternational Conference\\non Software Engineering®\\nHOME\\nNews from the SC\\nEDI STATEMENT\\nCONDUCT & SAFETY\\nHISTORY\\nPROCEEDINGS\\nINFLUENTIAL PAPERS\\nORGANIZING ICSE\\nSTEERING COMMITTEE\\nICSE SC Documents\\nSPONSORS\\nCONTACTS\\nLast updated\\nJan 2026\\nORGANIZING ICSE\\nFor over forty years, the International Conference on Software\\nEngineering (ICSE) has\\nserved as a premier forum for the presentation and exchange of the latest research results\\nand practical experiences in\\nsoftware engineering theories, methods, techniques, tools, and practices. To ensure the\\ncontinued excellence and success of\\nthe ICSE conference series, the ICSE Steering Committee (SC), ACM Special Interest Group in\\nSoftware Engineering (SIGSOFT),\\nIEEE-CS Technical Council on Software Engineering (TCSE), Association for Computing\\nMachinery, Inc. (ACM), and Institute of\\nElectrical and Electronics Engineers (IEEE), incorporated, through its IEEE Computer Society\\n(IEEE-CS) entered into a\\nMemorandum of Understanding (MOU). The purpose of the MOU is to define and clarify the\\nroles, authorities, responsibilities,\\nand key practices of the co-sponsors and the organizers of ICSE. This document also contains\\nICSE Operating Rules and Guidelines\\nthat constitute significant ICSE corporate knowledge to support ICSE continuity.\\nICSE Organizational Guidelines\\nICSE Operating\\nRules and Guidelines 2023 (24 pages pdf document)\\nCall for Letters of Interest to Host ICSE 2030.\\nCall for\\nLetters of Interest to Host ICSE 2030 (1 page pdf document)\\nOther useful documents:\\nICSE Duplicate Submission\\nStatement\\nICSE Awards and Plaques (PDF, PPT)\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-cf8967a02467e5aac69cec2e\", \"title\": \"ICSE SC Documents\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 36, \"end\": 1541, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 1505}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"ICSE\\nInternational Conference\\non Software Engineering®\\nHOME\\nNews from the SC\\nEDI STATEMENT\\nCONDUCT & SAFETY\\nHISTORY\\nPROCEEDINGS\\nINFLUENTIAL PAPERS\\nORGANIZING ICSE\\nSTEERING COMMITTEE\\nICSE SC Documents\\nSPONSORS\\nCONTACTS\\nLast updated\\nJan 2026\\nICSE SC Documents\\nThe following documents contain useful information for members of ICSE\\nOrganization and Program Committees. These documents embody significant ICSE corporate\\nknowledge to support ICSE continuity. More corporate ICSE knowledge can be found under Organizing ICSE.\\nICSE 2024 SC Strategic Discussions (PDF)\\nICSE\\n2019 PC Chairs Report by Bultan and Whittle (PDF)\\nICSE\\n2018 PC Chairs Report by Chechik, Harman, Zimmerman and Crnkovic (PDF)\\nICSE 2017 Report on the Technical Track V1.0 by Orso,\\nRobillard and Zimmermann (PDF)\\nICSE PC Chairs Guiding Document 1.1 by Canfora, Chechik,\\nCleland-Huang, van der Hoek, Robillard, Visser and Whittle (PDF)\\nICSE 2016 Insights and Lessons Learned from Analyzing ICSE\\n2016 by Visser and Williams (PDF)\\nICSE 2015 Report on Technical Track by Canfora and Elbaum\\n(PDF)\\nICSE\\n2014 Insights and Lessons Learned from Analyzing ICSE 2014 by Briand and van der Hoek\\n(PDF)\\nICSE 2008\\nWorkshop Report by Engels and Müller (PDF)\\nICSE 2005\\nFinal Report by Gruia-Catalin Roman (PDF)\\nICSE 2001\\nFinal Report by Müller, Harrold and Schäfer (PDF)\\nICSE 2001\\nPostmortem Report slides Müller, Harrold and Schäfer (PDF)\\nICSE 2000\\nFinal Report by Kevin Ryan (PDF)\\nICSE 2000\\nWorkshop Organization by Antonia Bertolino and Gail Murphy (HTML)\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-a9996aaca50aaf1f18002e6e\", \"title\": \"ICSE Home Page\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 30, \"end\": 1630, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 1600}], \"navigation_excerpt